finding: Medium — the new public explosion definition is not documented sufficiently for a stranger (src/standard/physics/runtime.ts:1011–1032). ExplosionDef's five fields have no field contracts. In particular nothing says falloff is an additional distance beyond radius, that maskBits filters shape category bits, or that impulses only apply to spheres, capsules and hulls. The latter is a silent exclusion in explosion.rs's proxy match, while explode's JSDoc promises bound dynamic shapes generally. Box3D types.h:1023–1041 explicitly documents the falloff and supported geometry; those contracts were lost at the public seam. The API also omits the finite/nonnegative radius/falloff preconditions enforced by WASM assertions. The numerical and scene checks can all pass with these public-contract gaps. Carry these semantics into the public JSDoc, narrowing the shape promise and stating refused inputs.
